A||||4||mrfixit58||Help ID this Thing... Please||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||04-19-2000||09:43 PM||||This is the kit car / re-body I mentioned in a note several weeks ago. I'm trying to find out more about it. It's built on a 87 GT 5-speed.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=446733&a=3289279" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=446733&a=3289279</A> <P>You may have to research old Kit Car Magazines. If anyone remembers seeing anything like it, please let me know.<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy L.||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||04-19-2000||10:27 PM||||Roy,<P>It got to be a one off body.<P>I have "The BIG book of Kit Cars, Past and Present" and it isn't in there that I can find.<P>Also, I have been with the Fieros since 1983 when I purchased my first 84 and I haven't every seen a kit like that one you displayed!<P>VERY INTERESTING!!!<P>It sort of looks like someone was trying to copy the 89 GT look.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||04-20-2000||09:03 AM||||You may be right. All I've been able to find out is the kit MAY have come from England. To me, it looks like they were trying to copy the 300ZX. <P>I was hoping the emblem would give a hint as to who made this car. It looked familiar to me but I can't seem to find it in my old Kit Car magazines.<P>I think what I may do from here is ask for help from Kit Car magazine. They will occationally publish pictures of mystery kits and ask their readers for help.<P>Regardless, I may not have the car long. I obtained it in a trade and really don't have time to fool with it. I may just unload it cheap and move on.<P>Thanks for your help,<BR>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||04-20-2000||09:34 AM||||Looks like it's missing some parts.  Hope you can get the parts if you decide to do it yourself.  I have no idea what it is, but I like the rear around the tail lights.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||04-20-2000||01:34 PM||||Monkeyman,<P>If your refering to the sail panel and the grill around the headlight, that's all supposed to be behind the seat and in the trunk. I say supposed because I haven't had time to look. It would be nice if all the parts were there but, those that may be missing look to fairly easy to replicate. <P>Again, I got this on trade and I felt if the only thing that came out of the car was the 5-speed then it was worth it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The body glass is very thin, maybe only two layers. I guess since the space frame does all the supporting, there wasn't much need for thick fiberglass. The areas inside the door jambs was another area they kinda took a short cut. The corners there aren't finished too well and you can peek between the sill and the fiberglass and see the ground.<P>I may get a battery and try to start it in a couple of weeks. Of course, before I turn the key, I'll need to buy new plugs, oil, and filter. If it runs, I'll be able to check out the transmission.<P>Originally, the Fiero came with the leather seats and they are still in fairly good shape. The only piece that needs work is the lumbar area of the driver's seat. The passenger's seat is perfect as is the drives seat cushion.<P>I think I got the better end of the deal. Although, he was awfully happy to see it go...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Roy L.||||reg||10
